      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2577462545,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The flip side of this is the search for actual usbll data, the filter is now  \n`len(usbll.data) > 1` instead of just the existence of `usbll.data` indicating data.  \n  \nWould it not be better to check for the data field when looking at ZLPs?  \n`usbll.data && len(usbll.data) != 192 && usbll.dst`  \n  \nOr as used to be spelled out in the WSUG (removed in !4737):  \n[6.4.7. A Common Mistake with !=](https://web.archive.org/web/20210204000447/https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html/#ChWorkBuildDisplayFilterMistake)  \n> If you want to filter out all packets containing IP datagrams to or from IP address 1.2.3.4, then the correct filter is !(ip.addr == 1.2.3.4) as it is read “show me all the packets for which it is not true that a field named ip.addr exists with a value of 1.2.3.4”, or in other words, “filter out all packets for which there are no occurrences of a field named ip.addr with the value 1.2.3.4”.  \n  \nSo the filter becomes `!(len(usbll.data) == 192) && usbll.dst`",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-22T18:16:55.938Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-22T19:51:28.617Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 287257847,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
