        {
          "id": 2577472648,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "`usbll.data` pretty much filters on DATA packets (be it DATA0, DATA1, DATA2, MDATA). What would be the use case for `len(usbll.data) > 1`? Why do you consider ZLP to be less important than other payloads? When there is ZLP, it always does indicate end of transaction.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6496125,
            "username": "desowin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tomasz Moń",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e423f0a8da1eede7f89748e5142d6915e4a636399964d35d888ed95ca85e2b50?s=80&d=identicon",
