        {
          "id": 2577476127,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "`SB1240-via-hub-HS-link.pcap` contained in `SB1240-via-hub_usbll.7z ` from https://wiki.wireshark.org/SampleCaptures#usb-link-layer contains usbll packets with zero length data.  \n  \nI don't work much with USB but trying to help with Discord question - https://discord.com/channels/889214182837321788/1385971581766860862 - which is a lua dissector for usbll_data.  \n  \nSo when looking at the pcap file above with a filter of `usbll.data` it was odd seeing `Data: <none>`. They are marked as `PID: DATA1 (0x4b)` but no data present. Is that normal or a weird capture?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-22T18:48:26.834Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-22T19:51:28.617Z",
