        {
          "id": 2577500148,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "https://www.usb.org/document-library/usb-20-specification  \n(usb_20_20240927/usb_20.pdf)  \n> 8.4.4 Data Packets  \n> A data packet consists of a PID, a data field containing zero or more bytes of data, and a CRC as shown in\nFigure 8-15.  \n  \n![250622_USBLL_DATA_zero_length_field](/uploads/2855d81a8dec8845f15fc1a6adf96b10/250622_USBLL_DATA_zero_length_field.png)  \n  \nI guess the change helps the dissector satisfy the spec but the logic in the filtering example would not have been enough for the change.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
